outputs.L1:
A method for manufacturing printed circuit boards includes the following steps:

a) inkjet printing a UV free-radical-curable inkjet ink onto a substrate (2);  
b) UV curing the inkjet ink on the inkjet-printed substrate; and  
c) thermally treating the UV-cured, inkjet-printed substrate;

wherein the UV free-radical-curable inkjet ink contains at least a colorant; a free-radical photoinitiator; a difunctional monomer or oligomer; a polyfunctional monomer or oligomer; and 1 to 15 wt% of a silane compound according to Formula (I),

wherein:

- the linking group L represents a —CH₂— group or an aliphatic chain having 2 to 10 carbon atoms, the aliphatic chain being optionally substituted by a nitrogen or oxygen atom;
- R¹ represents a methoxy group;
- R² and R³ independently represent a methoxy group or a C₁- to C₄-alkyl group; and
- R⁴ represents a functional group selected from the group consisting of an epoxy group, an amine group, a carbamate group, a trimethoxysilane group, and a ureido group.

outputs.L2:
A process for producing printed circuit boards comprises:

a) depositing a UV-curable, free-radical inkjet ink onto a substrate (2) by inkjet printing;  
b) exposing the printed substrate to UV radiation to cure the ink; and  
c) thermally treating the UV-cured, inkjet-printed substrate.

The ink comprises at least a colorant, a free-radical photoinitiator, a difunctional monomer or oligomer, a polyfunctional monomer or oligomer, and 1–15 wt% of a silane compound represented by Formula (I).

In Formula (I):

- the linking group L is either a —CH₂— group or an aliphatic chain containing 2–10 carbon atoms, with the chain optionally interrupted or substituted by nitrogen or oxygen;
- R¹ is a methoxy group;
- R² and R³ are each independently selected from a methoxy group and a C₁–C₄ alkyl group; and
- R⁴ is a functional group selected from an epoxy group, an amine group, a carbamate group, a trimethoxysilane group, and a ureido group.

counterfactuals.output:
1. **A method of manufacturing a printed circuit board, the method comprising:**  
providing a substrate having a conductive layer disposed on at least one surface thereof;  
inkjet-depositing, in accordance with a predetermined pattern, a UV-curable inkjet ink onto the conductive layer, the UV-curable inkjet ink comprising, based on a total weight of the ink, 1 wt% to 15 wt% of a functional silane compound;  
irradiating the deposited UV-curable inkjet ink with ultraviolet radiation to form a cured patterned layer; and  
processing the conductive layer using the cured patterned layer to define at least a portion of an electrical circuit on the substrate, thereby forming the printed circuit board.

1. **A method of manufacturing a printed circuit board, the method comprising:**

   providing a printed circuit board substrate;

   applying, in a predetermined pattern, a free-radical ultraviolet-curable ink onto at least a portion of a surface of the printed circuit board substrate, the ink comprising:  
   (a) a colorant;  
   (b) a photoinitiator;  
   (c) at least one difunctional free-radically polymerizable monomer or oligomer;  
   (d) at least one polyfunctional free-radically polymerizable monomer or oligomer having a functionality greater than two; and  
   (e) at least one silane compound of Formula (I); and

   exposing the applied ink to ultraviolet radiation to initiate free-radical polymerization of the monomers or oligomers and thereby form a cured ink layer adhered to the printed circuit board substrate.
